# ArxOS component registry: name  git-url  branch  [type]
#
# What arx reads:
#   name    arx health-checks the installed binaries of every name listed here.
#   url     used only by `arx sync`, which keeps git copies in ~/.cache/arxos/repos.
#   type    `bundled:<parent>` marks a component that ships inside another one's release.
#           `arx sync` skips it, and it counts as delivered whenever its parent is.
#           Other values (core, tool, kernel) are descriptive only.
#
# Installs and updates do not use git. They come from the R2 index (tools.json):
# `arx tools` and `arx update` download sha256-checked archives into ~/.cache/arxos/tools
# and run each one's install.sh. A name listed here with no index entry can never update,
# and `arx update` says so by name (ops::registry_drift).
#
# Delivered by another route, on purpose: linux-arxos (kernels go through `arx kernel` and
# the arxos-kernels manifest) and arxburn (it updates itself from its own releases).
# Not registered: wallpimp. It has no dist installer and no R2 index entry, and it is not in the
# image, so listing it only made every `arx update` report it as a tool that can never update.
# Re-add it here in the same change that publishes it to R2.
# Not registered: deathstroke. ArxOS does not ship it (2026-11-08) and it is delisted from the
# R2 index, so no ArxOS command can install it. It continues as its own project.
arx https://github.com/thearxos/arx-dist main core
arxctl https://github.com/thearxos/arxctl-dist main core
arxpods https://github.com/thearxos/arxctl-dist main bundled:arxctl
arxupd https://github.com/thearxos/arxupd-dist main core
anonkit https://github.com/thearxos/anonkit-dist main tool
droidB https://github.com/thearxos/droidB-dist main tool
arxguard https://github.com/thearxos/arxguard-dist main tool
arxos-greeter https://github.com/thearxos/arxos-greeter-dist main
arxos-browser https://github.com/thearxos/arxos-browser-dist main core
arxburn https://github.com/0xb0rn3/arxburn main tool
linux-arxos https://github.com/thearxos/linux-arxos-dist main kernel
